.TH smi-incoming-deploy "1" "September 2026" "SMI Toolset" "SMI Base Command"
.SH NAME
smi-incoming-deploy \- Hand incoming deployment packages to deployment plugins
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smi-incoming-deploy
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
.B smi-incoming-deploy
processes deployment packages dropped into the incoming directory: for every
.B .tar.gz
file in
.I /var/opt/setmy.info/incoming
it runs each executable
.B .sh
plugin from
.I /opt/setmy.info/lib/incoming
with the package path as the only argument.
What a package means is entirely up to the plugins.
.PP
A package whose name contains no plugin's pattern is not removed and not reported;
it stays in the incoming directory until a plugin handles it.
.SH PLUGINS
.PP
The plugins shipped are symbolic links to one generic script,
.IR /opt/setmy.info/lib/smi-incoming-deploy.sh .
The script takes its pattern from the name it was started under, the link name without
.BR .sh ,
and handles a package only when the package file name contains that pattern;
other packages are ignored with success.
A handled package is unpacked with
.B tar xzf
into
.IR /usr/share/nginx ,
the nginx content directory, creating the directory when it does not exist.
The archive paths are kept, so a package that contains
.I html/index.html
updates
.IR /usr/share/nginx/html/index.html .
After a successful unpack the package is removed from the incoming directory, so it is deployed
once and the
.B setmy-info-deploy.path
unit does not start the deployment again.
A package that matches but cannot be unpacked prints an error, exits with 1 and is kept in the
incoming directory for inspection.
When two links match the same package, the first one deploys and removes it; the next one
only warns that the file was not found.
.PP
Upload a package under a different name or directory and move it into the incoming directory
when it is complete: the watcher reacts to the file as soon as it exists, and a package that is
still being written fails to unpack.
.PP
Links created by the rpm and deb install scripts, and removed again on uninstall:
.TP
.I angular-start-project.sh
Deploys every incoming package whose file name contains
.BR angular-start-project ,
for example
.IR angular-start-project-1.0.0.tar.gz .
.PP
Another deployment only needs another link, named after the package it handles:
.RS
.nf
ln -s ../smi-incoming-deploy.sh /opt/setmy.info/lib/incoming/my-site.sh
.fi
.RE
.PP
The pattern is matched anywhere in the file name, so a link named
.I shop.sh
also handles
.IR webshop-2.0.tar.gz ;
choose names that are not part of other package names.
.PP
The command is quiet by design: a missing incoming directory, an empty one, or an absent
plugin directory all end with success, so it is safe to run from cron or a timer.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/opt/setmy.info/incoming
Incoming packages, one
.B .tar.gz
per deployment.
.TP
.I /opt/setmy.info/lib/incoming
Deployment plugins, executable
.B .sh
files; the shipped ones are links to
.IR smi-incoming-deploy.sh .
.TP
.I /opt/setmy.info/lib/smi-incoming-deploy.sh
Generic nginx deployment plugin, selected by the name of the link it is started through.
.TP
.I /usr/share/nginx
Target directory of the generic plugin.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Every plugin ran successfully, or there was nothing to do.
.TP
.I other
A plugin failed; the remaining packages are not processed.
.SH AUTHOR
Imre Tabur <imre.tabur@mail.ee>
